                </command><command>
                        <name>Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.OperationalData.PIEquipment_OP.OPModel.Commands.CreateProcessAdditionalProperties</name>
                        <shortname>CreateProcessAdditionalProperties</shortname>
                        <description>Creates extended process properties for the given piece of Equipment if none exists. List of properties:     - MinQuantity: The smallest quantity the piece of Equipment can handle.    - MinLevel: The smallest quantity which is recommended for the piece of Equipment.    - Quantity: The quantity that is stored in the piece of Equipment.    - MaxLevel: The biggest quantity recommended for the piece of Equipment.    - MaxQuantity: The biggest quantity the piece of Equipment can handle.    - IsSingleLot: A flag that indicates if the piece of Equipment should only handle a Material issued from a single lot.    - IsSingleMaterial: A flag that indicates if the piece of Equipment should only handle one kind of Material.    - AllocationStateMachineNId: The identifier of the State Machine on which the system will rely on, in order to manage the allocation state of the piece of Equipment.     - AllowedMaterialGroupNId: The Material Group allowed to be used with the piece of Equipment.    - AllowedMaterialNId: The Material allowed to be used with the piece of Equipment.   The command returns the following error codes in case of check failures: * 10300: the Equipment, identified by the given NId, does not exist; * 10992: the Equipment is frozen. </description>
                        <assembly>Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.OperationalData.PIEquipment_OP.OPModel.Commands, Version=1.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null</assembly>
                        <dotnetcommandtype></dotnetcommandtype>
                        <commandtype>Undefined</commandtype>
                        <domain>OperationalData</domain>
                        <visibility>Protected</visibility>
                        <composite>false</composite>
                        <taglist>
                        </taglist>
                        <securable>true</securable>
                        <handlers>
                                <handler>
                                        <name>Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.OperationalData.PIEquipment_OP.OPModel.Commands.CreateProcessAdditionalPropertiesHandlerShell</name>
                                        <assembly>Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.PIEquipment_OP.CommandHandler, Version=1.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null</assembly>
                                        <target_cpu>AnyCPU</target_cpu>
                                        <targetframework>netstandard2.0</targetframework>
                                        <dependencies></dependencies>
                                </handler>
                        </handlers>
                </command><command>
                        <name>Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.OperationalData.PIEquipment_OP.OPModel.Commands.AdjustEquipmentQuantity</name>
                        <shortname>AdjustEquipmentQuantity</shortname>
                        <description>Updates the Quantity stored in the Equipment. Checks if : - the given Equipment Id exists, otherwise it throws the error 10300 "Equipment with Id: { Id } does not exist."; - the given Equipment isn't frozen, otherwise it throws the error 10992 "Equipment with NId { Eqp.NId } is Frozen"; - the related ProcessAdditionalProperties exists, if it is the case, no error is thrown.</description>
                        <assembly>Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.OperationalData.PIEquipment_OP.OPModel.Commands, Version=1.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null</assembly>
